{
  "_comment": "Every rule table in shared/fixtures: which section holds which rule, who owns the rule, and which test suites must read it (kt: the companion's unit tests, lua: the plugin's tests, cpp: the Xteink host tests, py: the e2e kit's tests). Each suite fails when a section names it as a reader and none of its tests carries the mark '@fixture <file>#<section>' (or '@fixture <file>' for a whole file), or when it carries a mark the registry does not give it. The plugin's suite also fails on a fixture file or section with no row. A section is a key path ('mirror.due'); a row without one covers the whole file.",
